---
description: Watermark Pro project rules (applies to every file)
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md and PLAN.md before changing anything. Summary of the rules:

- Work in PLAN.md milestone order; certify each milestone before the next.
- Run `npm run quality` before declaring work done; report results honestly.
- Pin dependencies exactly after checking peer ranges; record in PLAN.md §3.1.
- No `any`, `!`, `@ts-ignore`, blanket eslint-disable, lowered thresholds, or
  `--legacy-peer-deps`. Suppressions need an inline reason and a PLAN.md §9 row.
- No dead code, no magic literals outside `src/shared/constants.ts`, no silent
  fallbacks, no mock data outside tests and e2e.
- Validate every boundary input with a Zod schema from `src/shared`.
- `erasableSyntaxOnly`: no enums, namespaces, or parameter properties.
- Update CHANGELOG.md (and PLAN.md when decisions change) with the code.
- Never modify global editor or agent settings from this repository.
